@startuml
!pragma layout smetana
title Layer 2.3 — proof submission and relay signal (built; evidence-only)

skinparam defaultFontName "Arial"
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundCorner 8
skinparam wrapWidth 240
skinparam sequence {
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #EEF2FF
  ParticipantBorderColor #4F46E5
  LifeLineBorderColor #94A3B8
}
autonumber

participant "Student phone\n(browser)" as Phone
participant "Express API" as API
participant "MongoDB" as DB

note over Phone
  The phone decoded a session, wave and key.
  The private P-256 key never leaves IndexedDB.
end note

Phone -> Phone: Build canonical message\nbioattend-proof:v1|session=…|wave=…|key=…|student=…
Phone -> Phone: Sign with the bound device key
Phone -> API: POST /api/v1/check-in-sessions/:id/proofs\n{ wave, key, signature }\n(cookie session)

API -> API: Origin guard · auth · student role\n60 proofs/min per student
API -> DB: Load session and check\nactive roster · approved binding\n· no pending device change
API -> API: Verify signature with the\nbound public key
API -> DB: Find existing proof for\n(session, student, wave)

alt Exact retry
  API -> DB: If this wave is still pending,\npromote it atomically
  API --> Phone: 200\nduplicate: true · attendanceDecided: false\nnext: server-minted relay signal when one is live
else New proof — current round, key fresh and matching
  API -> DB: Insert evidence + signature +\nprotocol version (unique per student/wave)
  API -> DB: Mint pending K(n+1)\nwith a two-minute lifetime
  DB --> API: Stored, TTL ~24 h
  API --> Phone: 201\nrecorded: true · duplicate: false\nattendanceDecided: false\nnext: K(n+1)
else New proof — pending round, key fresh and matching
  API -> DB: Insert evidence + signature
  API -> DB: Atomically promote pending K(n+1)\narchive the old key, mint pending K(n+2)
  API --> Phone: 201\nrecorded: true · duplicate: false\nattendanceDecided: false\nnext: K(n+2)
else Invalid, stale, wrong device or rate limited
  API --> Phone: 400 / 401 / 403 / 409 / 429
end

Phone -> Phone: Play the returned signal 2-3 times\nthen listen again automatically

note over API, DB
  No score, attendance flag or ID round.
  The signed proof binds the submission to the bound account/device.
  It does not prove the phone was physically inside the room.
  The server mints every relay key; phones never invent one.
  A student may try the displayed round through +2 because the
  frame carries only the key; the server accepts only its
  current or pending pair.
  The teacher can advance manually only after accepted evidence;
  a fresh pending key keeps its original expiry.
  A closed session returns neither current key nor pending state.
end note

@enduml
